eparately.  Thus the Utopians and the Christians, although having some common beliefs, are each given a section. The followers of Karl Marx, the acknowledged orthodox Socialists, and the disciples of Edward Bernstein, the avowed revisionists, are treated separately.\" - Summary by Ted Lienhart &amp; E. C. Robbins<br /><br />For further information, including links to online text, reader information, RSS feeds, CD cover or other formats (if available), please go to the <a href=\"https://librivox.org/socialism-by-various/\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">LibriVox catalog page</a> for this recording.<br /><br />For more free audio books or to become a volunteer reader, visit <a href=\"https://librivox.org/\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">librivox.org</a>.<br />","language":"eng","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/","mediatype":"audio","subject":"librivox; audiobooks;economics; socialism; political science","title":"Socialism","collection":["librivoxaudio","audio_bookspoetry"],"uploader":"info@librivox.org","collection_added":"audio_bookspoetry","publicdate":"2026-09-03 10:23:10","addeddate":"2026-09-03 10:23:10"},"server":"ia800500.us.archive.org","uniq":1107168368,"workable_servers":["ia800500.us.archive.org","ia600500.us.archive.org"]}